The committed geoCreator version (by the duplicate agent, commit 0d65d9a) deviates from upstream: it merges echartsStyle into ALL regions, including explicitly declared ones (merge with `zrUtil.merge(regionOption, style)` — since merge without overwrite doesn't override existing keys, explicit region options still win for keys they declare; echartsStyle only fills missing keys like `label`).

Upstream's version (3ec7b26) only applies echartsStyle to regions NOT explicitly declared. Hmm wait — actually let me double check upstream: in upstream 3ec7b26's geoCreator:

```ts
        zrUtil.each(source.regions, function (region) {
            const name = region.name;
            if (!dataNameMap.get(name)) {
                const regionOption = {
                    name: name
                };
                // apply specified echarts style in GeoJSON data
                const specifiedGeoJSONRegionStyle = ...
                specifiedGeoJSONRegionStyle && zrUtil.merge(regionOption, specifiedGeoJSONRegionStyle);
                regionsArr.push(regionOption);
            }
        });
```

Yes — upstream only merges for undeclared regions. The committed version here merges for all, but with merge semantics (declared keys win). Is that "wrong"? Arguably it's a superset: echartsStyle fills defaults even for declared regions (label from GeoJSON applies when the region option doesn't specify label). The requirement says "while still allowing chart configuration to build on top of those defaults where appropriate" — this behavior actually satisfies that too, and preserves explicit options.

